 "poem": "The current world with many\nHallows and hinds, many\nBishops and choirs of young women\nIn troupes and handsome bands;\nSoon I shall say the few things about\nA word they have forgotten.  Instead\nI'll tell you all you can do about\nThe people who came in times before.\nThe old bird perched on our\nTree's limb; 'tis a little,\nComposed as it was, so aloneed and\nTo me for any one.",
